  "finalText": "I built the toggle in the 800×600 comp, 2 s at 60 fps, and checked it in a contact sheet. The first render showed a stray blue fill inside the checkmark, which I removed. The re-check shows the right frames; I didn't scrub through every frame.\n\n- **Off state:** it sits still until 0.4 s with a grey **Track** (`#c7c7cc`) and the white knob on the left.\n- **Knob slide:** at 0.4 s the **Knob** glides right and overshoots by about 10 px. It settles at 1.2 s, exactly on the right-hand end.\n- **Squash and stretch:** the knob stretches to 124% wide and 88% tall mid-travel, then squashes to 92% wide and 108% tall on arrival. It relaxes to 100% by 1.2 s.\n- **Track colour:** it crossfades from grey to iOS green (`#34c759`) between 0.4 and 0.8 s.\n- **Checkmark:** a green stroke inside the knob draws itself on from 0.75 to 1.05 s, so it appears just as the knob lands.\n\nI can add a soft knob shadow, make the squash bouncier, or loop it back to off for a continuous demo."
